  "details": "Since VRCSDK 3.7.6, there is a bug where if the scale of a parent or child object containing a PhysBone component is changed, the PhysBone continues to rotate until it reaches its limit angle.\n\nThis issue is still present in VRCSDK 3.8.0 and persists even after today's update.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1.Create an object and add a PhysBone component to it.\n\n2.Set a limit angle for the PhysBone.\n\n3.Upload the avatar and test it in VRChat.\n\n4.Use a Float parameter to control Motion Time and modify the Y-axis scale of the parent or child object in-game.\n\n5.Observe that the PhysBone rotates continuously until it reaches its limit angle.\n\nExpected behavior:\n\nThe PhysBone should not continue rotating uncontrollably when the scale of the parent or child object is modified.\n\nThis issue affects avatar dynamics and can cause unintended behavior in various use cases. Please investigate and provide a fix.",
